## Active Sprint

> **→ active:** `docs/sprint/SPRINT-NNN-<slug>.md`   ·   or **— none —** between sprints.
>
> **Parallel streams?** (optional) — a repo running two work streams holds one active sprint EACH:
> one pointer line per stream, prefixed with the stream name (matching the sprint's `stream:`
> frontmatter). Single-stream repos keep the one unprefixed pointer above — nothing changes.
> **→ [stream-a]:** `docs/sprint/SPRINT-NNN-<slug>.md`
> **→ [stream-b]:** `docs/sprint/SPRINT-MMM-<slug>.md`
>
> The active sprint is its own working doc (`templates/SPRINT.md.template`). `/lean-doc-generator
> promote` creates it from the Backlog; `/orchestrator sprint-bulk` loops its Plan DoD; `/lean-doc-generator
> close` writes its Retro. This section is only the pointer(s) — task detail lives in the sprint file.

